;; =======================================================
;; MAP DRAW (BLITZ MODE)
;; =======================================================
;; StampPlayfield{} runs once per playfield bitmap, from InitLevel{}, and nothing re-reads mapBuffer after that, so a change to
;; mapBuffer during play is seen by later readers but not on screen. QueueMetatileRedraw{} and RedrawMetatileCells{} put such changes
;; on screen: a list of changed cells, drawn into both playfield bitmaps.

;; Cut tile tileNow from the atlas into #TILE_SHAPE. The caller then Uses its own bitmap and Blocks or Blits it.
;; WaitBlitter first, here and before every GetaShape of a shape a blit may still be reading: GetaShape frees the shape's memory and
;; allocates it again cleared (MEMF_CLEAR, by the CPU) before it waits for the blitter (shapeslib.ab3, do_GetaShape; bitmaplib.ab3,
;; extbitmap), and a Block returns as soon as the blitter starts. Without the wait, a Block of a shape followed by a GetaShape of it
;; turns the planes the blitter has not yet read into 0: one plane of one cell missing in one bitmap, a flickering block or stray rows.
Statement CutAtlasTile{tileNow.w}
  Use BitMap #ATLAS_BM
  ; The last Block may still be reading #TILE_SHAPE (above).
  WaitBlitter
  GetaShape #TILE_SHAPE, (tileNow MOD #LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*#TILE, (tileNow/#LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*#TILE, #TILE, #TILE
End Statement

;; Stamp one map cell into drawBitmap, from mapBuffer.
;;
;; GID 0 paints sky rather than doing nothing. The full playfield gets its sky
;; from the Cls in StampPlayfield{}, but a per-cell repaint has no Cls, so a cell
;; that goes empty -- a shattered brick -- has to be cleared explicitly.
Statement StampMetatileCell{cellIndex.w}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), mapWidth, drawBitmap
  SHARED mapGid, mapPixelX, mapPixelY
  mapGid = mapBuffer(cellIndex)
  mapPixelX = (cellIndex MOD mapWidth)*#TILE
  mapPixelY = (cellIndex/mapWidth)*#TILE
  If mapGid = 0
    Boxf mapPixelX, mapPixelY, mapPixelX + #TILE - 1, mapPixelY + #TILE - 1, 0
    Statement Return
  EndIf
  CutAtlasTile{mapGid - 1}
  Use BitMap drawBitmap
  Block #TILE_SHAPE, mapPixelX, mapPixelY
End Statement

;; The cells of the map grouped by tile: stampHead(gid) is the first cell holding that GID and
;; stampNext(cell) the next one, -1 at the end. Empty cells (GID 0) are in no list. Built once
;; for both bitmaps.
Statement BuildStampLists{}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), stampHead(), stampNext(), stampSkipped
  stampSkipped = 0
  For gidIndex.w = 0 To #STAMP_GID_MAX
    stampHead(gidIndex) = -1
  Next
  For cellIndex.w = #MAP_CELLS - 1 To 0 Step -1
    gidNow.w = mapBuffer(cellIndex)
    If gidNow > #LOOK_FRONT_TILES Then stampSkipped = stampSkipped + 1
    If gidNow > 0 AND gidNow <= #LOOK_FRONT_TILES
      stampNext(cellIndex) = stampHead(gidNow)
      stampHead(gidNow) = cellIndex
    EndIf
  Next
End Statement

;; The map into drawBitmap from the lists: sky by the Cls, then each tile cut from the atlas once per bitmap
;; and blocked into every cell that holds it (the main project's TIMING note).
Statement StampPlayfield{}
  SHARED mapWidth, drawBitmap, stampHead(), stampNext()
  Use BitMap drawBitmap
  Cls 0
  For gidIndex.w = 1 To #STAMP_GID_MAX
    cellNow.w = stampHead(gidIndex)
    If cellNow >= 0
      tileNow.w = gidIndex - 1
      CutAtlasTile{tileNow}
      Use BitMap drawBitmap
      While cellNow >= 0
        Block #TILE_SHAPE, (cellNow MOD mapWidth)*#TILE, (cellNow/mapWidth)*#TILE
        cellNow = stampNext(cellNow)
      Wend
    EndIf
  Next
End Statement

;; What the back bitmap holds, as a number: the scenery kind, and in the All-Stars look the tile set's, which has its own strip of that kind (the hills' in the
;; overground, the cave wall in the underground). The NES look's is the kind alone (its tile set is always 0).
Function.w BackKindOf{sceneryNow.w, setNow.w}
  If sceneryNow = #SCENERY_NONE Then Function Return(sceneryNow)
  Function Return(sceneryNow + setNow*8)
End Function

;; The GID of one cell of a scenery kind's back strip. The NES look has its three strips in the area table (backStrip()). The All-Stars look has the
;; one the user composed (allstarsBackStrip(), sparkydave.allstars-palette.data.ab3: hills and clouds on one strip, one speed) and gives it to the
;; hills kind, the main level's; the other kinds show no back yet.
Function.w BackStripGid{stripKind.w, stripCell.w}
  SHARED backStrip(), allstarsBackStrip(), allstarsBackStripUnder(), allstarsBackStripWater(), allstarsBackStripCastle()
  If #LOOK_ALLSTARS = 1
    ; The overground's strip is every ground area's: 1-1's hills and clouds, and the clouds and trees kinds of 1-3, 2-1 and 2-3 (their NES strips are the cartridge's own pictures).
    If stripKind = #SCENERY_HILLS OR stripKind = #SCENERY_CLOUDS OR stripKind = #SCENERY_TREES Then Function Return allstarsBackStrip(stripCell)
    If stripKind = BackKindOf{#SCENERY_HILLS, #TILE_SET_UNDERGROUND} Then Function Return allstarsBackStripUnder(stripCell)
    If stripKind = BackKindOf{#SCENERY_WATER, #TILE_SET_WATER} Then Function Return allstarsBackStripWater(stripCell)
    If stripKind = BackKindOf{#SCENERY_CLOUDS, #TILE_SET_CASTLE} Then Function Return allstarsBackStripCastle(stripCell)
    Function Return 0
  EndIf
  Function Return backStrip(stripKind*#BACK_CELLS + stripCell)
End Function

;; The back playfield: the strip of a scenery kind from backStrip() (the area table), sky by the
;; palette's pen 0 as everywhere else, stamped into the back bitmap and again after the strip's own width on, so a view that
;; starts near the strip's end reads on into the copy. The kinds: clouds, hills, trees (#SCENERY_*; the main project's AMIGA_RENDERER note,
;; "The back playfield by scenery"). A visible, not-yet-stamped kind is a few frames' work (a tile cut for each cell), so it is
;; done behind a cover.
Statement StampBackPlayfield{kind.w}
  SHARED backStampedKind, hudMirrorStale, pageScreenDrawn(), backStampHead(), backStampNext()
  Use BitMap #BACK_BM
  Cls 0
  ; The back bitmap is cleared: whatever the overlay's pages held is gone (TakeBackAsCanvas{} does it too, and comes first when an overlay leaves).
  pageScreenDrawn(0) = #SCREEN_NONE
  pageScreenDrawn(1) = #SCREEN_NONE
  ;; The cells are grouped by tile first, as the map's stamp does (BuildStampLists{}), so each tile is cut from the atlas once. Cutting
  ;; at each change of tile along the strip costs 37 to 62 frames at a pipe for the All-Stars cave wall, which has a different tile in
  ;; nearly every cell.
  ;; The strip's first #BACK_HUD_ROWS rows are never stamped, whatever a strip holds there: while Mario is above the view the tall list
  ;; shows the HUD's copy in the back bitmap's rows 0 to 15 and two empty rows after it (HudEnd strings, lines 16 and 17), so a picture
  ;; there would show round the HUD.
  For gidIndex.w = 0 To #STAMP_GID_MAX
    backStampHead(gidIndex) = -1
  Next
  For backCell.w = #BACK_CELLS - 1 To #BACK_STRIP_W*#BACK_HUD_ROWS Step -1
    backGid.w = BackStripGid{kind, backCell}
    If backGid > 0 AND backGid <= #LOOK_ATLAS_TILES AND backGid <= #STAMP_GID_MAX
      backStampNext(backCell) = backStampHead(backGid)
      backStampHead(backGid) = backCell
    EndIf
  Next
  ; Each tile cut once and blocked into every cell that holds it, and again one strip on where the view's wrap reads it.
  For gidIndex.w = 1 To #STAMP_GID_MAX
    backCell = backStampHead(gidIndex)
    If backCell >= 0
      CutAtlasTile{gidIndex - 1}
      Use BitMap #BACK_BM
      While backCell >= 0
        backX.w = (backCell MOD #BACK_STRIP_W)*#TILE
        backY.w = (backCell/#BACK_STRIP_W)*#TILE
        Block #TILE_SHAPE, backX, backY
        If backX < #VIEW_W + #FETCH_GUARD Then Block #TILE_SHAPE, backX + #BACK_STRIP_W*#TILE, backY
        backCell = backStampNext(backCell)
      Wend
    EndIf
  Next
  backStampedKind = kind
  ; The Cls took the HUD's copy in rows 0 to 15 with it (UpdateHudMirror{} makes it again).
  hudMirrorStale = True
End Statement

;; Whether the back needs stamping for an area of this scenery when it holds that of `stamped`: only for a kind that shows
;; (an area with none shows no back, the palette hides it, and the bitmap is left as it is: a trip to a bonus room does not
;; cost a restamp of the hills on the way back).
Function.w BackStripNeeded{scenery.w, stamped.w}
  If scenery = #SCENERY_NONE Then Function Return False
  If scenery = stamped Then Function Return False
  Function Return True
End Function

;; The area on show has its strip in the back bitmap. Called from StampBothPlayfields{} (every area change and restart) and at
;; start.
Statement EnsureBackStrip{}
  SHARED currentAreaScenery, backStampedKind, tileSetShown, currentAreaType
  ; The All-Stars sky bonus (a ground area with no scenery) has the main level's sky bands, which the back would show through (its pens are one colour): its back is left blank.
  If #LOOK_ALLSTARS = 1 AND currentAreaScenery = #SCENERY_NONE AND currentAreaType = #AREA_TYPE_GROUND AND backStampedKind <> 0
    StampBackPlayfield{0}
    Statement Return
  EndIf
  backKindWanted.w = BackKindOf{currentAreaScenery, tileSetShown}
  If BackStripNeeded{backKindWanted, backStampedKind} = True
    StampBackPlayfield{backKindWanted}
    MarkTransition{"EnsureBackStrip: the back strip stamped"}
  EndIf
End Statement

;; The one place the rule lives: whatever uses the back bitmap as a canvas (the title and pause overlays) calls this, and the bitmap no
;; longer holds any kind's strip, so the next area to show one stamps it. (Called from the places that draw an overlay into it.)
Statement TakeBackAsCanvas{}
  SHARED backStampedKind, hudMirrorStale, pageScreenDrawn()
  backStampedKind = -1
  ; Whatever the overlay's pages held is not on them now (or is about to go): both are drawn whole next.
  pageScreenDrawn(0) = #SCREEN_NONE
  pageScreenDrawn(1) = #SCREEN_NONE
  hudMirrorStale = True
End Statement

;; The title or pause overlay has been used the back as its canvas and goes: the area's strip back over it, behind the cover (or,
;; for an area that shows none, the bitmap is left and counted as holding no kind).
Statement RestoreBackStrip{}
  TakeBackAsCanvas{}
  EnsureBackStrip{}
End Statement

;; The attract mode's scenery: while the title is up the back
;; playfield is the title's canvas, so the clouds and hills are stamped into the world bitmaps
;; instead, in the map's empty cells, repeated every #BACK_STRIP_W columns along the level, as the
;; cartridge's own 1-1 has them. Into both bitmaps, after a fresh StampBothPlayfields{}; the game's
;; reload (RestartLevel{}) stamps them plain again.
Statement StampAttractScenery{}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), mapWidth, areaColumns
  ; The All-Stars strip's cells are pens for the back playfield, not the front's: no scenery in the attract mode's front under that look yet.
  If #LOOK_ALLSTARS = 1 Then Statement Return
  AutoCookie Off
  lastTile.w = -1
  For backCell.w = 0 To #BACK_CELLS - 1
    backGid.w = BackStripGid{#SCENERY_HILLS, backCell}
    backRow.w = backCell/#BACK_STRIP_W
    If backGid > 0 AND backGid <= #LOOK_ATLAS_TILES AND backRow < #MAP_H
      backTile.w = backGid - 1
      If backTile <> lastTile
        CutAtlasTile{backTile}
        lastTile = backTile
      EndIf
      Use BitMap #PLAY_BM_A
      For mapColumn.w = backCell MOD #BACK_STRIP_W To areaColumns - 1 Step #BACK_STRIP_W
        If mapBuffer(backRow*mapWidth + mapColumn) = 0 Then Block #TILE_SHAPE, mapColumn*#TILE, backRow*#TILE
      Next
      Use BitMap #PLAY_BM_B
      For mapColumn.w = backCell MOD #BACK_STRIP_W To areaColumns - 1 Step #BACK_STRIP_W
        If mapBuffer(backRow*mapWidth + mapColumn) = 0 Then Block #TILE_SHAPE, mapColumn*#TILE, backRow*#TILE
      Next
    EndIf
  Next
  AutoCookie On
End Statement

;; The word the stamp writes at one 16 px word of the world: the atlas tile's word for that pixel row and plane, or 0 for an
;; empty cell and for one the stamp does not draw (a GID past #LOOK_FRONT_TILES, which only the Cls has written).
Function.w StampWantedWord{wordColumn.w, pixelRow.w, wordPlane.w}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), mapWidth
  wantedGid.w = mapBuffer((pixelRow/#TILE)*mapWidth + wordColumn)
  If wantedGid < 1 OR wantedGid > #LOOK_FRONT_TILES Then Function Return 0
  atlasStruct.l = Addr BitMap(#ATLAS_BM)
  atlasPlane.l = Peek.l(atlasStruct + 8 + wordPlane*4)
  atlasRow.l = ((wantedGid - 1)/#LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*#TILE + (pixelRow MOD #TILE)
  Function Return Peek.w(atlasPlane + atlasRow*Peek.w(atlasStruct) + ((wantedGid - 1) MOD #LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*2)
End Function

; Debug mode: one repaired word kept for the bitmap check report, with what each world bitmap held there before the repair.
Statement KeepStampRepair{wordColumn.w, pixelRow.w, wordPlane.w, wantedNow.w, wordA.w, wordB.w}
  SHARED debugMode, mapBuffer(), mapWidth, stampCheckTotal, stampWordCount, stampWordStamp(), stampWordColumn(), stampWordRow()
  SHARED stampWordPlane(), stampWordKnown(), stampWordWanted(), stampWordFoundA(), stampWordFoundB()
  If debugMode = False Then Statement Return
  If stampWordCount >= #STAMP_CHECK_WORDS Then Statement Return
  stampWordStamp(stampWordCount) = stampCheckTotal
  stampWordColumn(stampWordCount) = wordColumn
  stampWordRow(stampWordCount) = pixelRow
  stampWordPlane(stampWordCount) = wordPlane
  stampWordKnown(stampWordCount) = True
  If mapBuffer((pixelRow/#TILE)*mapWidth + wordColumn) > #LOOK_FRONT_TILES Then stampWordKnown(stampWordCount) = False
  stampWordWanted(stampWordCount) = wantedNow
  stampWordFoundA(stampWordCount) = wordA
  stampWordFoundB(stampWordCount) = wordB
  stampWordCount = stampWordCount + 1
End Statement

;; A word missing at missingAddress went out with another high word (RepairStampedBitmaps{} says why), so its copy is a whole
;; multiple of 64 KB away. Each such address inside either world bitmap, in the rows and columns the stamp draws, is set to what
;; the stamp wants there if it holds anything else. Returns how many words it put right.
Function.w RepairMovedCopies{missingAddress.l, lastColumn.w}
  worldBytesPerRow.l = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A))
  planeBytes.l = #WATCH_PIXEL_ROWS*worldBytesPerRow
  repairedCount.w = 0
  For copyStep.w = -32 To 32
    If copyStep <> 0
      stepBytes.l = copyStep
      copyAddress.l = missingAddress + stepBytes*65536
      For copyPlane.w = 0 To #PLAYFIELD_PLANES - 1
        planeStartA.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A) + 8 + copyPlane*4)
        planeStartB.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_B) + 8 + copyPlane*4)
        copyOffset.l = -1
        If copyAddress >= planeStartA AND copyAddress < planeStartA + planeBytes Then copyOffset = copyAddress - planeStartA
        If copyAddress >= planeStartB AND copyAddress < planeStartB + planeBytes Then copyOffset = copyAddress - planeStartB
        If copyOffset >= 0
          copyRow.w = copyOffset/worldBytesPerRow
          copyColumn.w = (copyOffset MOD worldBytesPerRow)/2
          If copyColumn <= lastColumn
            wantedNow.w = StampWantedWord{copyColumn, copyRow, copyPlane}
            If Peek.w(copyAddress) <> wantedNow
              KeepStampRepair{copyColumn, copyRow, copyPlane, wantedNow, Peek.w(planeStartA + copyOffset), Peek.w(planeStartB + copyOffset)}
              Poke.w copyAddress, wantedNow
              repairedCount = repairedCount + 1
            EndIf
          EndIf
        EndIf
      Next
    EndIf
  Next
  Function Return repairedCount
End Function

;; After every stamp, in every build: repair stray one-pixel rows. A blit's last D write can land between the two halves of the next
;; blit's long write to BLTDPT (the 68020 writes the high word first), so it goes out with the next plane's high word: the word is
;; missing where it belongs and turns up a whole multiple of 64 KB away. It is rare, and was caught by the stamp check. A Block's blit
;; of a plane ends at its tile's last row, so a moved word is always missing from a cell's row 15: only those rows are compared, both
;; bitmaps a long at a time (right after a stamp they are the same), each word that differs is set to what the stamp wants, and its
;; copy is looked for and put right (RepairMovedCopies{}). Checking every row of the whole area takes 65 to 69 frames a stamp; this is
;; a sixteenth of the reads. Not repaired: a word of 0 moved (nothing is missing where it belongs; where it lands on a stamped tile, a
;; hole), a word wrong the same way in both bitmaps, and a copy outside the bitmaps, in other Chip RAM. In debug mode each repair is
;; kept for the bitmap check report.
Statement RepairStampedBitmaps{}
  SHARED debugMode, mapWidth, areaColumns, currentLevel, currentArea, currentAreaType, tileSetJustChanged
  SHARED stampCheckTotal, stampBadCount, stampBadNumber(), stampBadLevel(), stampBadArea(), stampBadType()
  SHARED stampBadSetChanged(), stampBadWords()
  ; The stamp's last Block may still be writing: read only what it has finished.
  WaitBlitter
  stampCheckTotal = stampCheckTotal + 1
  setChanged.w = tileSetJustChanged
  tileSetJustChanged = False
  differCount.l = 0
  lastColumn.w = areaColumns - 1
  If lastColumn > mapWidth - 1 Then lastColumn = mapWidth - 1
  worldBytesPerRow.l = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A))
  For checkPlane.w = 0 To #PLAYFIELD_PLANES - 1
    planeA.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A) + 8 + checkPlane*4)
    planeB.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_B) + 8 + checkPlane*4)
    For cellRow.w = 0 To #MAP_H - 1
      pixelRow.w = cellRow*#TILE + #TILE - 1
      rowA.l = planeA + pixelRow*worldBytesPerRow
      rowB.l = planeB + pixelRow*worldBytesPerRow
      For pairColumn.w = 0 To lastColumn Step 2
        If Peek.l(rowA + pairColumn*2) <> Peek.l(rowB + pairColumn*2)
          For wordColumn.w = pairColumn To pairColumn + 1
            wordA.w = Peek.w(rowA + wordColumn*2)
            wordB.w = Peek.w(rowB + wordColumn*2)
            If wordColumn <= lastColumn AND wordA <> wordB
              wantedNow.w = StampWantedWord{wordColumn, pixelRow, checkPlane}
              KeepStampRepair{wordColumn, pixelRow, checkPlane, wantedNow, wordA, wordB}
              differCount = differCount + 1
              If wordA <> wantedNow
                Poke.w rowA + wordColumn*2, wantedNow
                differCount = differCount + RepairMovedCopies{rowA + wordColumn*2, lastColumn}
              EndIf
              If wordB <> wantedNow
                Poke.w rowB + wordColumn*2, wantedNow
                differCount = differCount + RepairMovedCopies{rowB + wordColumn*2, lastColumn}
              EndIf
            EndIf
          Next
        EndIf
      Next
    Next
  Next
  If differCount = 0 OR debugMode = False Then Statement Return
  If stampBadCount >= #STAMP_CHECK_STAMPS Then Statement Return
  stampBadNumber(stampBadCount) = stampCheckTotal
  stampBadLevel(stampBadCount) = currentLevel
  stampBadArea(stampBadCount) = currentArea
  stampBadType(stampBadCount) = currentAreaType
  stampBadSetChanged(stampBadCount) = setChanged
  stampBadWords(stampBadCount) = differCount
  stampBadCount = stampBadCount + 1
End Statement

;; Stamp both playfield bitmaps from the current mapBuffer, pairing drawBuffer
;; with drawBitmap so UnBuffer operates on the correct bob buffer. Shared by
;; init.blitz.ab3 (load time) and ResetLevel{} (F1 restore) so the protocol
;; cannot drift between the two paths. After stamping, re-initialises both
;; bob buffers so UnBuffer{} does not restore stale pre-reset backgrounds.
Statement StampBothPlayfields{}
  SHARED drawBitmap, drawBuffer, warpZoneState, warpCameraLocked, scrollLockLifted, castleTextDrawnA, castleTextDrawnB
  ; The area's back strip first (an unchanged kind costs nothing), all behind the cover the caller has up.
  EnsureBackStrip{}
  ;; A stamp paints the text over, so the warp zone's is drawn again when the screen next reaches it (and its camera lock is
  ;; taken again then).
  warpZoneState = 0
  warpCameraLocked = False
  ; A castle's scroll lock is on again (a restart is before the axe).
  scrollLockLifted = False
  ; The stamp has painted over the castle's messages: drawn again if still wanted.
  castleTextDrawnA = 0
  castleTextDrawnB = 0
  AutoCookie Off
  BuildStampLists{}
  MarkTransition{"StampBothPlayfields: tile lists built"}
  drawBitmap = #PLAY_BM_A
  drawBuffer = #BOB_BUF_A
  StampPlayfield{}
  MarkTransition{"StampBothPlayfields: first bitmap stamped"}
  drawBitmap = #PLAY_BM_B
  drawBuffer = #BOB_BUF_B
  StampPlayfield{}
  MarkTransition{"StampBothPlayfields: second bitmap stamped"}
  ;; Re-seed both bob buffers with the freshly stamped background. Buffer{}
  ;; copies the current bitmap contents into the bob buffer, so any stale
  ;; saved sprites or pre-reset tiles are discarded -- without this, UnBuffer
  ;; in the next DrawFrame{} restores old art over the reset map.
  Buffer #BOB_BUF_A, #BOB_BYTES
  Buffer #BOB_BUF_B, #BOB_BYTES
  AutoCookie On
  MarkTransition{"StampBothPlayfields: bob buffers seeded"}
  ; The two bitmaps compared and any stray repaired, whole area (after the buffers, which allocate Chip RAM, so they are covered too).
  RepairStampedBitmaps{}
  MarkTransition{"StampBothPlayfields: stamp repaired"}
End Statement

;; Mark a map cell for repaint. Deduped, so a cell queued twice in one round
;; drains once: the bump path queues its cell on the clear and again on the
;; settle, 16 frames apart, and nothing else should queue the same cell twice
;; either. This list is small, so the dedupe is cheap insurance.
;; Over-full is dropped rather than wrapped: a stale tile is a better failure than
;; losing the frame.
Statement QueueMetatileRedraw{cellIndex.w}
  SHARED redrawCell(), redrawCount, redrawDoneA, redrawDoneB
  If redrawCount >= #MAX_REDRAW_CELLS Then Statement Return
  If redrawCount > 0
    For queueIndex = 0 To redrawCount - 1
      If redrawCell(queueIndex) = cellIndex Then Statement Return
    Next
  EndIf
  redrawCell(redrawCount) = cellIndex
  redrawCount = redrawCount + 1
  ;; A new cell invalidates whatever the bitmaps were already owed, so neither
  ;; counts as done until it has been repainted in this round.
  redrawDoneA = False
  redrawDoneB = False
End Statement

;; Repaints the queued cells into the CURRENT bitmap only, and keeps the queue until both bitmaps have had it.
;; Painting both and forgetting would leave the other bitmap's bob buffer holding stale saved art. Its
;; UnBuffer would later restore that art over the repainted cell, leaving a block fragment in the sky.
;;
;; Repainting lazily, into whichever bitmap is about to be drawn into, cannot
;; flicker: the other bitmap is not on screen while it is stale, and by the time
;; it is displayed it has been repainted. And it cannot go stale, because
;; UnBuffer runs BEFORE this and DrawPlayer runs after, so the stale restore is
;; covered immediately and the cookie is re-saved fresh on top of it.
Statement RedrawMetatileCells{}
  SHARED redrawCell(), redrawCount, drawBitmap, redrawDoneA, redrawDoneB
  If redrawCount = 0 Then Statement Return
  Use BitMap drawBitmap
  AutoCookie Off
  For drainIndex = 0 To redrawCount - 1
    StampMetatileCell{redrawCell(drainIndex)}
  Next
  AutoCookie On
  If drawBitmap = #PLAY_BM_A
    redrawDoneA = True
  Else
    redrawDoneB = True
  EndIf
  If redrawDoneA = True
    If redrawDoneB = True
      redrawCount = 0
      redrawDoneA = False
      redrawDoneB = False
    EndIf
  EndIf
End Statement

;; Whether a word of $FFFF in one world bitmap is a stray: the other bitmap's word there (otherWord) is what the map wants, and the
;; other planes agree in both bitmaps at that word (a bob differs in more than one). The word wanted is left in strayWanted. A cell
;; StampPlayfield{} does not stamp (a GID past #LOOK_FRONT_TILES), or a column past the map, is never one.
Function.w IsStrayWord{wordColumn.w, pixelRow.w, wordPlane.w, otherWord.w}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), mapWidth, strayWanted
  If wordColumn > mapWidth - 1 Then Function Return False
  suspectGid.w = mapBuffer((pixelRow/#TILE)*mapWidth + wordColumn)
  If suspectGid > #LOOK_FRONT_TILES Then Function Return False
  strayWanted = 0
  If suspectGid > 0
    atlasPlane.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#ATLAS_BM) + 8 + wordPlane*4)
    atlasRow.l = ((suspectGid - 1)/#LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*#TILE + (pixelRow MOD #TILE)
    strayWanted = Peek.w(atlasPlane + atlasRow*Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#ATLAS_BM)) + ((suspectGid - 1) MOD #LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*2)
  EndIf
  If otherWord <> strayWanted Then Function Return False
  worldOffset.l = pixelRow*Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A)) + wordColumn*2
  For planeIndex.w = 0 To #PLAYFIELD_PLANES - 1
    If planeIndex <> wordPlane
      wordA.w = Peek.w(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A) + 8 + planeIndex*4) + worldOffset)
      wordB.w = Peek.w(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_B) + 8 + planeIndex*4) + worldOffset)
      If wordA <> wordB Then Function Return False
    EndIf
  Next
  Function Return True
End Function

;; F10 in debug mode, two checks (the hunt for the stray one-pixel rows, the main project's candidates notes). The view's cells in both world bitmaps
;; against the atlas tiles mapBuffer says they hold, word by word: a cell is 16 px wide from x 0, so each of its rows in a plane is
;; exactly one word, and the word wanted is the atlas's at the tile's place (0 for an empty cell). Anything drawn on the world
;; differs too: an enemy, a coin, the bumped block, the warp zone's text, a cell still queued for its repaint. Then the whole area,
;; both bitmaps compared a long at a time, for strays (IsStrayWord{}) anywhere in it, in view or not. Read through the Blitz BitMap
;; objects: bytes a row at 0, the plane pointers from 8 (InitBand{} reads the back's the same way). All kept for the report at exit
;; (WriteBitmapCheckReport{}). A cell StampPlayfield{} does not stamp (a GID past #LOOK_FRONT_TILES) is not checked, and only counted.
Statement CheckWorldBitmaps{}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), mapWidth, areaColumns, cameraX, currentLevel, currentArea, drawBitmap, redrawCount, strayWanted
  SHARED checkPressCount, checkWordCount, checkPressLevel(), checkPressArea(), checkPressCamera(), checkPressDrawBitmap()
  SHARED checkPressQueued(), checkPressWords(), checkPressSkipped(), checkWordPress(), checkWordBitmap(), checkWordColumn()
  SHARED checkWordRow(), checkWordPlane(), checkWordWanted(), checkWordFound()
  SHARED checkPressStrays(), checkStrayCount, checkStrayPress(), checkStrayBitmap(), checkStrayColumn(), checkStrayRow()
  SHARED checkStrayPlane(), checkStrayWanted()
  If checkPressCount >= #BITMAP_CHECK_PRESSES Then Statement Return
  pressIndex.w = checkPressCount
  checkPressCount = checkPressCount + 1
  checkPressLevel(pressIndex) = currentLevel
  checkPressArea(pressIndex) = currentArea
  checkPressCamera(pressIndex) = Int(cameraX)
  checkPressDrawBitmap(pressIndex) = drawBitmap
  checkPressQueued(pressIndex) = redrawCount
  differCount.l = 0
  skippedCount.w = 0
  atlasBytesPerRow.l = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#ATLAS_BM))
  firstColumn.w = Int(cameraX)/#TILE
  lastColumn.w = firstColumn + #VIEW_W/#TILE
  If lastColumn > mapWidth - 1 Then lastColumn = mapWidth - 1
  For checkBitmap.w = #PLAY_BM_A To #PLAY_BM_B
    worldBytesPerRow.l = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(checkBitmap))
    For checkPlane.w = 0 To #PLAYFIELD_PLANES - 1
      worldPlane.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(checkBitmap) + 8 + checkPlane*4)
      atlasPlane.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#ATLAS_BM) + 8 + checkPlane*4)
      For checkRow.w = 0 To #MAP_H - 1
        For checkColumn.w = firstColumn To lastColumn
          checkGid.w = mapBuffer(checkRow*mapWidth + checkColumn)
          If checkGid > #LOOK_FRONT_TILES
            If checkBitmap = #PLAY_BM_A AND checkPlane = 0 Then skippedCount = skippedCount + 1
          Else
            atlasWord.l = 0
            If checkGid > 0
              atlasWord = atlasPlane + (((checkGid - 1)/#LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*#TILE)*atlasBytesPerRow + ((checkGid - 1) MOD #LOOK_ATLAS_COLS)*2
            EndIf
            worldWord.l = worldPlane + (checkRow*#TILE)*worldBytesPerRow + checkColumn*2
            For cellRow.w = 0 To #TILE - 1
              wantedNow.w = 0
              If atlasWord <> 0 Then wantedNow = Peek.w(atlasWord + cellRow*atlasBytesPerRow)
              foundNow.w = Peek.w(worldWord + cellRow*worldBytesPerRow)
              If foundNow <> wantedNow
                differCount = differCount + 1
                If checkWordCount < #BITMAP_CHECK_MAX
                  checkWordPress(checkWordCount) = pressIndex
                  checkWordBitmap(checkWordCount) = checkBitmap
                  checkWordColumn(checkWordCount) = checkColumn
                  checkWordRow(checkWordCount) = checkRow*#TILE + cellRow
                  checkWordPlane(checkWordCount) = checkPlane
                  checkWordWanted(checkWordCount) = wantedNow
                  checkWordFound(checkWordCount) = foundNow
                  checkWordCount = checkWordCount + 1
                EndIf
              EndIf
            Next
          EndIf
        Next
      Next
    Next
  Next
  checkPressWords(pressIndex) = differCount
  checkPressSkipped(pressIndex) = skippedCount
  ; The whole area, for strays.
  strayCount.w = 0
  lastColumn = areaColumns - 1
  If lastColumn > mapWidth - 1 Then lastColumn = mapWidth - 1
  worldBytesPerRow = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A))
  For pixelRow.w = 0 To #WATCH_PIXEL_ROWS - 1
    For checkPlane = 0 To #PLAYFIELD_PLANES - 1
      rowA.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A) + 8 + checkPlane*4) + pixelRow*worldBytesPerRow
      rowB.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_B) + 8 + checkPlane*4) + pixelRow*worldBytesPerRow
      For pairColumn.w = 0 To lastColumn Step 2
        If Peek.l(rowA + pairColumn*2) <> Peek.l(rowB + pairColumn*2)
          For wordColumn.w = pairColumn To pairColumn + 1
            wordA.w = Peek.w(rowA + wordColumn*2)
            wordB.w = Peek.w(rowB + wordColumn*2)
            strayBitmap.w = -1
            If wordA = -1 AND wordB <> -1
              If IsStrayWord{wordColumn, pixelRow, checkPlane, wordB} = True Then strayBitmap = #PLAY_BM_A
            EndIf
            If wordB = -1 AND wordA <> -1
              If IsStrayWord{wordColumn, pixelRow, checkPlane, wordA} = True Then strayBitmap = #PLAY_BM_B
            EndIf
            If strayBitmap >= 0
              strayCount = strayCount + 1
              If checkStrayCount < #BITMAP_CHECK_STRAYS
                checkStrayPress(checkStrayCount) = pressIndex
                checkStrayBitmap(checkStrayCount) = strayBitmap
                checkStrayColumn(checkStrayCount) = wordColumn
                checkStrayRow(checkStrayCount) = pixelRow
                checkStrayPlane(checkStrayCount) = checkPlane
                checkStrayWanted(checkStrayCount) = strayWanted
                checkStrayCount = checkStrayCount + 1
              EndIf
            EndIf
          Next
        EndIf
      Next
    Next
  Next
  checkPressStrays(pressIndex) = strayCount
End Statement

;; A word of $FFFF that WatchWorldBitmaps{} found in one world bitmap and not the other, and IsStrayWord{} passes: a candidate. A
;; moving object with a row of one colour passes that too (1-2's lifts, for one), so a candidate is a stray only when it is
;; seen again in the same place a sweep later: a stray stays until it is scrolled off, a moving row has gone. A new candidate is
;; kept with the frame its row was last seen clean (-1: its row not looked at since the watch went on; -2: looked at, but not
;; this column) and a copy of the ring, oldest frame first, in a free slot or one whose candidate was not seen again within two
;; sweeps.
Statement WatchSuspect{suspectBitmap.w, wordColumn.w, pixelRow.w, wordPlane.w, otherWord.w}
  SHARED cameraX, watchFrame, watchRing(), watchFoundCount, watchFoundTotal, watchFoundFrame(), strayWanted
  SHARED watchFoundSince(), watchFoundBitmap(), watchFoundColumn(), watchFoundRow(), watchFoundPlane(), watchFoundWanted()
  SHARED watchFoundCamera(), watchFoundRing(), watchFoundConfirmed(), watchConfirmedTotal
  SHARED watchRowFrame(), watchRowFirst(), watchRowLast()
  If IsStrayWord{wordColumn, pixelRow, wordPlane, otherWord} = False Then Statement Return
  ; Already a candidate here: seen again on a later sweep, it is a stray.
  foundIndex.w = 0
  If watchFoundCount > 0
    For foundIndex = 0 To watchFoundCount - 1
      If watchFoundBitmap(foundIndex) = suspectBitmap AND watchFoundColumn(foundIndex) = wordColumn
        If watchFoundRow(foundIndex) = pixelRow AND watchFoundPlane(foundIndex) = wordPlane
          If watchFoundConfirmed(foundIndex) = 0 AND watchFoundFrame(foundIndex) < watchFrame
            watchFoundConfirmed(foundIndex) = watchFrame
            watchConfirmedTotal = watchConfirmedTotal + 1
          EndIf
          Statement Return
        EndIf
      EndIf
    Next
  EndIf
  watchFoundTotal = watchFoundTotal + 1
  ; A free slot, else one whose candidate was not seen again within two sweeps.
  slotIndex.w = -1
  If watchFoundCount < #WATCH_MAX
    slotIndex = watchFoundCount
    watchFoundCount = watchFoundCount + 1
  Else
    For foundIndex = 0 To #WATCH_MAX - 1
      If slotIndex < 0 AND watchFoundConfirmed(foundIndex) = 0
        If watchFrame - watchFoundFrame(foundIndex) > 2*#WATCH_PIXEL_ROWS/#WATCH_ROWS_A_FRAME Then slotIndex = foundIndex
      EndIf
    Next
  EndIf
  If slotIndex < 0 Then Statement Return
  foundIndex = slotIndex
  sinceFrame.l = watchRowFrame(pixelRow)
  If sinceFrame >= 0
    If wordColumn < watchRowFirst(pixelRow) OR wordColumn > watchRowLast(pixelRow) Then sinceFrame = -2
  EndIf
  watchFoundConfirmed(foundIndex) = 0
  watchFoundFrame(foundIndex) = watchFrame
  watchFoundSince(foundIndex) = sinceFrame
  watchFoundBitmap(foundIndex) = suspectBitmap
  watchFoundColumn(foundIndex) = wordColumn
  watchFoundRow(foundIndex) = pixelRow
  watchFoundPlane(foundIndex) = wordPlane
  watchFoundWanted(foundIndex) = strayWanted
  watchFoundCamera(foundIndex) = Int(cameraX)
  For ringIndex.w = 0 To #WATCH_RING - 1
    ringFrom.l = ((watchFrame + 1 + ringIndex) MOD #WATCH_RING)*#WATCH_FIELDS
    ringTo.l = (foundIndex*#WATCH_RING + ringIndex)*#WATCH_FIELDS
    For fieldIndex.w = 0 To #WATCH_FIELDS - 1
      watchFoundRing(ringTo + fieldIndex) = watchRing(ringFrom + fieldIndex)
    Next
  Next
End Statement

;; Once a frame from the main loop while the watch is on (F10 in debug mode): the frame's state into the ring, then
;; #WATCH_ROWS_A_FRAME of the world's pixel rows, both bitmaps compared a long at a time, from the view's left across the view and
;; #WATCH_AHEAD_COLUMNS more (a stray can be written ahead of the view and first seen as it scrolls in). Where
;; they differ, a word of $FFFF in one of them goes to WatchSuspect{}. So a stray in that span is first seen within a sweep (120
;; frames) of being written, and the ring holds what happened in between. Each row keeps the frame it was looked at and the columns
;; it covered. The ring's numbers, in order: the frame, the camera, Mario's x and y, his state, big, lifeEvent, the area, the bitmap
;; drawn into, the bump (on, its cell), and the objects, debris sets, fireballs and floaters active, and the cells queued for a
;; repaint.
Statement WatchWorldBitmaps{}
  SHARED watchOn, watchFrame, watchFramesOn, watchNextRow, watchRowFrame(), watchRowFirst(), watchRowLast(), watchRing()
  SHARED mapWidth, cameraX, coverKind
  SHARED playerX, playerY, playerState, playerIsBig, lifeEvent, currentArea, drawBitmap, blockBumpActive, blockBumpCell
  SHARED objActive(), debrisActive(), fireballActive(), floaterActive(), redrawCount
  If watchOn = False Then Statement Return
  watchFrame = watchFrame + 1
  watchFramesOn = watchFramesOn + 1
  ringAt.w = (watchFrame MOD #WATCH_RING)*#WATCH_FIELDS
  watchRing(ringAt) = watchFrame
  watchRing(ringAt + 1) = Int(cameraX)
  watchRing(ringAt + 2) = playerX
  watchRing(ringAt + 3) = playerY
  watchRing(ringAt + 4) = playerState
  watchRing(ringAt + 5) = playerIsBig
  watchRing(ringAt + 6) = lifeEvent
  watchRing(ringAt + 7) = currentArea
  watchRing(ringAt + 8) = drawBitmap
  watchRing(ringAt + 9) = blockBumpActive
  watchRing(ringAt + 10) = blockBumpCell
  activeCount.w = 0
  For slotIndex.w = 0 To #MAX_OBJECTS - 1
    If objActive(slotIndex) <> False Then activeCount = activeCount + 1
  Next
  watchRing(ringAt + 11) = activeCount
  activeCount = 0
  For slotIndex = 0 To #DEBRIS_SETS - 1
    If debrisActive(slotIndex) <> False Then activeCount = activeCount + 1
  Next
  watchRing(ringAt + 12) = activeCount
  activeCount = 0
  For slotIndex = 0 To #FIREBALL_SLOTS - 1
    If fireballActive(slotIndex) <> 0 Then activeCount = activeCount + 1
  Next
  watchRing(ringAt + 13) = activeCount
  activeCount = 0
  For slotIndex = 0 To #FLOATER_SLOTS - 1
    If floaterActive(slotIndex) <> False Then activeCount = activeCount + 1
  Next
  watchRing(ringAt + 14) = activeCount
  watchRing(ringAt + 15) = redrawCount
  If coverKind <> #COVER_NONE Then Statement Return
  firstColumn.w = Int(cameraX)/#TILE
  firstColumn = firstColumn - (firstColumn MOD 2)
  lastColumn.w = firstColumn + #VIEW_W/#TILE + #WATCH_AHEAD_COLUMNS + 1
  If lastColumn > mapWidth - 1 Then lastColumn = mapWidth - 1
  worldBytesPerRow.l = Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A))
  For rowStep.w = 0 To #WATCH_ROWS_A_FRAME - 1
    pixelRow.w = watchNextRow
    watchNextRow = watchNextRow + 1
    If watchNextRow >= #WATCH_PIXEL_ROWS Then watchNextRow = 0
    For planeIndex.w = 0 To #PLAYFIELD_PLANES - 1
      rowA.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_A) + 8 + planeIndex*4) + pixelRow*worldBytesPerRow
      rowB.l = Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#PLAY_BM_B) + 8 + planeIndex*4) + pixelRow*worldBytesPerRow
      For pairColumn.w = firstColumn To lastColumn Step 2
        If Peek.l(rowA + pairColumn*2) <> Peek.l(rowB + pairColumn*2)
          For wordColumn.w = pairColumn To pairColumn + 1
            wordA.w = Peek.w(rowA + wordColumn*2)
            wordB.w = Peek.w(rowB + wordColumn*2)
            If wordA <> wordB
              If wordA = -1 Then WatchSuspect{#PLAY_BM_A, wordColumn, pixelRow, planeIndex, wordB}
              If wordB = -1 Then WatchSuspect{#PLAY_BM_B, wordColumn, pixelRow, planeIndex, wordA}
            EndIf
          Next
        EndIf
      Next
    Next
    watchRowFrame(pixelRow) = watchFrame
    watchRowFirst(pixelRow) = firstColumn
    watchRowLast(pixelRow) = lastColumn + 1
  Next
End Statement

;; Restore the level to its initial state: blocks, items, player position.
;; Called from ReadControls{} on F1. The buffers were snapshotted at startup in
;; sparkydave.init.blitz.ab3, so this copies them back and re-stamps the
;; playfields. The caller is responsible for re-drawing the player afterwards,
;; because DrawPlayer{} lives in sparkydave.player.blitz.ab3 which is included
;; after this file -- calling it here would be a forward reference.
Statement ResetLevel{}
  SHARED mapBuffer(), mapBufferBackup(), metatileBuffer(), metatileBufferBackup()
  SHARED objActive(), objType(), objVelY(), objRiseRemaining(), objRiseStep()
  SHARED objRiseTarget(), objFractionY(), objSourceCell(), objPopTimer()
  SHARED cameraX, debrisActive(), debrisNextSet, floaterActive(), stompChain
  SHARED multiCoinStarted(), multiCoinIntervals(), intervalPhase
  SHARED hiddenBlockLive(), hiddenOneUpFlag, fireballActive(), fireballCounter, playerThrowTimer
  SHARED playerStarIntervals, playerHidden, poleNumberShown, endTask, fireworkActive()
  SHARED currentArea, areaEvent, pipeOccludeCols, currentAreaType, startAreaType, currentAreaScenery, startAreaScenery
  SHARED drawBitmap, drawBuffer, redrawCount, redrawDoneA, redrawDoneB
  SHARED vineColumnX, playerClimbing, climbAutoUp, climbAreaChange, vineWalkOut, playerCrouching, castleEndTask, bridgeCollapseStep
  SHARED castleWalkReady, castleTextWanted, castleMessageTicks, warpPipeTaken, warpLevelTarget
  MarkTransition{"ResetLevel: begin"}
  warpPipeTaken = -1
  warpLevelTarget = -1
  ; No vine, and not on one (the area is made again): the sky bonus's own is started after, by its way in.
  vineColumnX = -1
  ;; Not crouching: the cartridge clears its RAM when an area starts (InitializeArea), and the crouch only follows Down while he is on the
  ;; ground, so a big Mario who went down a pipe crouching fell into the bonus room still crouched.
  playerCrouching = False
  playerClimbing = False
  climbAutoUp = False
  climbAreaChange = False
  vineWalkOut = False
  For copyCell = 0 To #MAP_CELLS - 1
    mapBuffer(copyCell) = mapBufferBackup(copyCell)
    metatileBuffer(copyCell) = metatileBufferBackup(copyCell)
  Next
  redrawCount = 0
  redrawDoneA = False
  redrawDoneB = False
  For copyCell = 0 To #DEBRIS_SETS - 1
    debrisActive(copyCell) = False
  Next
  debrisNextSet = 0
  stompChain = 0
  For copyCell = 0 To #FLOATER_SLOTS - 1
    floaterActive(copyCell) = False
  Next
  For copyCell = 0 To #MAX_MULTI_COINS - 1
    multiCoinStarted(copyCell) = False
    multiCoinIntervals(copyCell) = 0
  Next
  intervalPhase = #INTERVAL_PERIOD - 1
  For copyCell = 0 To #FIREBALL_SLOTS - 1
    fireballActive(copyCell) = 0
  Next
  fireballCounter = 0
  playerThrowTimer = 0
  ;; The Starman is not cleared here: a pipe or a vine to another area keeps it (the cartridge clears StarInvincibleTimer only when a new
  ;; level's timer is fetched, Entrance_GameTimerSetup, smbdis 2873); a restart, a death and the title clear it themselves.
  playerHidden = False
  currentArea = #AREA_MAIN
  currentAreaType = startAreaType
  currentAreaScenery = startAreaScenery
  areaEvent = 0
  pipeOccludeCols = 0
  poleNumberShown = False
  endTask = 0
  castleEndTask = 0
  bridgeCollapseStep = 0
  castleWalkReady = False
  castleTextWanted = 0
  castleMessageTicks = 0
  For copyCell = 0 To #FIREWORK_SLOTS - 1
    fireworkActive(copyCell) = False
  Next
  ; Hidden blocks are built again as the screen reaches them, if the flag allows.
  For copyCell = 0 To #MAX_HIDDEN_BLOCKS - 1
    hiddenBlockLive(copyCell) = False
  Next
  If #HIDDEN_ONEUP_ONCE = 0 Then hiddenOneUpFlag = True
  ; Clear all pool slots
  For copyCell = 0 To #MAX_OBJECTS - 1
    objActive(copyCell) = False
    objType(copyCell) = #OBJ_NONE
    objVelY(copyCell) = 0
    objRiseRemaining(copyCell) = 0
    objRiseStep(copyCell) = 0
    objRiseTarget(copyCell) = 0
    objFractionY(copyCell) = 0
    objSourceCell(copyCell) = 0
    objPopTimer(copyCell) = 0
  Next
  cameraX = 0
  MarkTransition{"ResetLevel: cells and objects cleared"}
  ;; The state only: the caller stamps the playfields (StampBothPlayfields{}) when it is done
  ;; with the map, so the way into the bonus room, which loads another map, does not stamp the
  ;; main level for nothing. Then DrawPlayer{} runs in DrawFrame{} next tick, so the reset
  ;; buffer is ready before the player is drawn into it.
End Statement

;; END OF MAP DRAW (BLITZ MODE)
